          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "num:233 GB",
            "num:850 GB",
            "entity:DeepSeek",
            "entity:Flash"
          ],
          "narration": "You're picking between two DeepSeek downloads tonight. The Pro's smallest published file is eight hundred fifty gigabytes on disk. The Flash's smallest is two hundred thirty-three gigabytes on your drive."
        },
        {
          "id": "s03",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 11.4,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Hugging Face",
            "entity:Unsloth"
          ],
          "narration": "Both are quantized, stored at lower precision to shrink the file. One file each. Both ship as a single-file build you can run tonight. Unsloth publishes them on Hugging Face, fully open weights."
        },
        {
          "id": "s04",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 14.1,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:Active parameters"
          ],
          "narration": "Each is a mixture of experts, a model that wakes only a slice of itself per word. Those active parameters, the slice that does the work, stay small. Every expert still has to sit on your drive or in your memory."
        },
        {
          "id": "s05",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 13.8,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Flash",
            "entity:Unsloth"
          ],
          "narration": "So what fits tonight? Drive streaming, pulling parts of the model from your fast drive into memory when they are needed, is the trick. On Unsloth's numbers, a big Spark-class machine holds the Flash. Nothing published yet holds the Pro."
        },
        {
          "id": "s06",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 15.9,
          "specific": false,
          "hits": [],
          "narration": "Picture a master carpenter with a rolling tool chest. The daily tools ride inside; the rare ones fetch from the store across the street, your drive. Except a router inside the model picks per word, and the fetch costs seconds instead of a trip across town."
        },
        {
          "id": "s07",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 12.1,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:DeepSeek",
            "entity:Flash",
            "entity:Terminal"
          ],
          "narration": "Here's the twist. On DeepSeek's own table, the Flash scores ninety point six on the terminal bench, ahead of the Pro. The smaller pull is the quality pick for coding and agents, not the compromise."
        },
        {
          "id": "s08",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 10.7,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:DeepSeek",
            "entity:Flash"
          ],
          "narration": "The Pro still leads the world-knowledge rows, where its bigger backbone earns its keep. And if you ever rent these in DeepSeek's cloud, the Flash is the cheaper seat there too."
        },
        {
          "id": "s09",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 12.4,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Unsloth"
          ],
          "narration": "So tonight: count your free memory. Grab the Unsloth single-file build that fits. Run it in llama dot cpp or Unsloth Desktop. Let your drive hold the overflow. Set reasoning effort to trade speed against depth."
        },
        {
          "id": "s10",
          "role": "payoff_close",
          "est_duration_s": 5.2,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:Flash"
          ],
          "narration": "The rule to keep: your free memory picks the model. Tonight, it picks the Flash."
        }
      ]
